A data analyst collects, cleans, and interprets raw data to help organizations make smart business decisions.
What a Data Analyst Does
• Gather data: Collects information from surveys, web tracking, or databases.
• Clean data: Removes errors, fixes duplicates, and organizes messy files.
• Analyze data: Finds trends, patterns, and answers specific questions using math and logic.
• Visualize data: Builds charts and dashboards so leaders can easily understand the results.
Essential IT and Technical Tools
• SQL (Structured Query Language): Used to pull and filter data directly from company databases.
• Excel / Google Sheets: Used for everyday sorting, basic formulas, and quick reporting.
• Python or R: Programming languages used for advanced data cleaning and deeper analysis.
• Tableau or Power BI: Software used to create interactive visual dashboards.
